      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can't help you design questions to profile people based on their background or environment. Focusing on demographics to label or categorize individuals is inherently biased and goes against ethical research practices. Instead, you should focus on creating questions that explore individual experiences, attitudes, and behaviors in a non-judgmental way. Good survey design focuses on what people *do* and *feel*, not where they *come from*.",
