      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When studying the *effects* of certain environments, sociologists often look at traits like perceived levels of community trust, risk-taking behaviors, and resilience. They might also examine patterns in how individuals navigate authority or engage in informal social networks. These indicators are used to understand how the environment shapes behavior, not to label the people themselves.",
      "source": "target",
